; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR TETRIS  -  steer the falling pieces, clear the rows   (loads at $4000-$5FFF)
; ==========================================================================
; Load, cold-boot, press SPACE (or a digit 0-9 to start at that level).
; Left/right arrows (or a d) move the piece, up (or w) rotates it, z rotates it
; back, down (or s) moves it down one row, SPACE drops it. A full row clears:
; 10 / 30 / 50 / 80 points for 1-4 rows at once, times (level + 1). Every 10 rows
; the level goes up and the pieces fall faster. When a new piece has no room at
; the top the game is over. P pauses, ESC quits; SPACE plays again. BEST is kept
; while it runs.
;
; The well is its own picture: each row is stored as the bytes the terminal is
; sent, and the same bytes are the collision grid. The falling piece is drawn from
; relative-move shape strings, so a move patches 4 digits of one cursor address.
; FIT's four READIDX bases are rewritten by the program when the piece turns.
;
; VT100: cursor addressing, cursor down/left/right, backspace, erase to end of
; line, hide/show cursor, reverse video (title). No scrolling.
;
; VERIFICATION (Firmware-Math/tetris_verify.py, V0061.34): PASS 2026-09-29 - 3 games x 200
;   autopilot pieces checked against a Python model after every key (well in memory,
;   the piece, every cell on screen, score/lines/level), letter+arrow pairs under UART
;   overrun, all 7 pieces rotated both ways at both walls (kicks), gravity at levels
;   0-9, pause, game over, key flush, SPACE again, ESC quit, rerun without reloading.
; HW-VERIFIED on the Elf2K (V0061.34), 2026-09-29 - Craig: "Tetris works great!"
;
; 684 STELLAR commands.
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

; D 4000 CD             START
; D 4001 F2 02          SETSIZE 02                         two 4 KB blocks: $4000-$5FFF
; D 4003 11 0B 00 00    LOADXI R11 0000                    RB = 0: the index for variables and patching strings
; D 4007 11 0C 18 DC    LOADXI R12 18DC
; D 400B 11 0A 00 00    LOADXI R10 0000
; D 400F 3A 02 AC       COPYXMY R10 -> M(R12)              BEST = 0 (each time the program starts)
; D 4012 10 00 00       LOADAI 0000
; D 4015 2F 0B 18 D2    WRITEIDX R11 18D2                  start at level 0 unless a digit picks another
; D 4019 11 0E 14 F8    LOADXI R14 14F8
; D 401D C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 401F BD 07 90       CALL MENU                          SPACE or 0-9 starts (a lone ESC quits)
; NEW:
